ks after v2.3.1 deploy - rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the latest deploy (v2.3.1; v2.3.1-rc also unhealthy). Error rate was 0.18. Action taken: rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release with healthy status, in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator partial_failure, leaving the service mixed across versions; a retry completed successfully. Current state: all regions on v2.3.0, healthy=true, error rate 0.002. Follow-up: investigate the v2.3.1 failure root cause, the orchestrator partial failure, and decide when v2.3.1 can be redeployed.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.0-sev2-2025"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), and it's healthy again with an error rate of 0.002, down from 0.18.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.1 and v2.3.1-rc were both unhealthy, so I picked v2.3.0, the most recent release marked healthy. The first attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator partial failure, which left the service mixed across versions. I retried the same rollback and it completed in all regions.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 for checkout-api, and it paged the on-call engineer. The first request timed out, so I retried with the same idempotency key. The incident was opened once.\n- **Follow-up:** The incident summary lists the next steps: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, look into the orchestrator partial failure, and decide when v2.3.1 can be redeployed.", "type": "text"}]}]}